  "findings": [
    "Current BA-ITA JSON distinguishes Year 1 60 EC and Year 2 40+20 EC. Year 3 has a 5 EC Renaissance seminar, a nominal 15 EC restricted group, a 10 EC thesis and 30 EC open choice. Four restricted modules have the exact same codes as compulsory Year 2 modules. Only 5603ICLCY supplies a distinct listed 5 EC.",
    "The programme-specific 2026–2027 regulation URL returns an access-block HTML page. The official prospective study programme confirms the language/literature/linguistics/culture structure and 30 EC open space, but its linked diagram is for 2025–2026 and does not establish a current cohort substitution.",
    "5601VIWY supplies an explicit replacement for two previous 5 EC linguistics modules. It requires an introductory linguistics pass. That bridge does not resolve third-year choices. 5603ICMSY in the first semester requires 5 EC prior specified Italian linguistics/history/sociolinguistics and high Italian and oral English proficiency. 5603ICLNY requires B2 Italian. The current Lingua italiana IIa goals include B1/B2 productive skills, so progression is not established for every entrant by catalogue placement alone.",
    "5603VBSCRY verifies 10 EC and a required thesis seminar. It requires first year and 40 EC from second year including legacy IIa–IId language courses. The current list gives Lingua italiana IIa and IIb, 10 EC each. Obtain authoritative current-cohort equivalence rather than assuming it from totals.",
    "Six direct generators cover acquisition, linguistics and language history, literature, cultural history and their integration. Rows 13470–13481 are supporting topics. Italian film study is directly taught in 5603ICLNY and therefore row 13485 is support-only. Thesis-in-Italian remains a study illustration pending exact rule. Outcomes remain context, without a guaranteed qualification."
  ],
